body:
This problem was [observed in #4099](https://github.com/mlpack/mlpack/pull/4099#discussion_r2869765283).  The following code fails:

```c++
#include <mlpack.hpp>

using namespace mlpack;

int main()
{
  // download coco.names from http://models.mlpack.org/yolo/coco.names
  arma::mat dataset;
  TextOptions opts = CSV + Fatal + Categorical;
  Load("coco.names", dataset, opts);
```

However, this should not fail: we are explicitly saying the format is CSV, and so regardless of the extension, we should load the file:

<img width="1454" height="315" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/458fe4dc-4d05-44df-a857-5f20d7049c20" />

so if `AutoDetect` (the default format) is *not* specified, then the extension should not be used.

I found that the cause of the bug is that the extension is explicitly checked in `LoadCategorical()` so that we can dispatch to either the CSV or ARFF loader, but the fix is straightforward: just use `opts.Format()` instead of the filename extension.  That is the guts of this fix, but there were a number of other things that needed to be done along the way:

 * To properly handle the TSV case, instead of "piggybacking" onto CSVs, we need to introduce a new format `TSVASCII`.  The reason we have to do this is because Armadillo does not support `csv_opts` for TSV files; thus, a separate format is necessary so that `LoadDense()` does not try to load a TSV with `csv_opts` (which will succeed but only give one row in the resulting matrix).
 
 * Next we have the problem that when `AutoDetect` is used, we inspect the file and determine its type, including determining whether it has semicolons, but then we don't actually update the `DataOptions` object (but we should).  So, `GuessFileType()` and `DetectFileType()` had to be changed to explicitly take a `DataOptions` object and update its `Semicolon()` member if needed.

 * `doc/user/load_save.md` documents `ModelOptions` but `ModelOptions` does not exist!  So I removed it and adapted the documentation to suggest that users should use the base `DataOptions` instead when loading models.
 
 * The documentation had some typos that I found and was using incorrect names for some of the types and methods.  Easy fixes.
 
 * I moved `LoadCategorical()` into `load_categorical.hpp` where it seems like it should belong.  (Note that there are some changes to that function, sorry that the diff will be a little difficult to see exactly what changed.)

