When file validation failed (bad extension or size > 5MB), `handleFileSelect` returned early without resetting the `<input type="file">` value. The browser suppresses `change` events when the same file is re-selected, so the user was silently stuck — unable to retry with the same file.

## Changes

- **`DashboardPage.tsx`** — Clear `fileInputRef.current.value` before each early `return` in the validation branches:

```tsx
if (!['docx', 'pdf', 'txt', 'rtf'].includes(ext || '')) {
  setUploadError('Unsupported file type. Accepted: .docx, .pdf, .txt, .rtf');
  if (fileInputRef.current) fileInputRef.current.value = '';  // added
  return;
}
if (file.size > 5 * 1024 * 1024) {
  setUploadError('File too large. Maximum size is 5MB.');
  if (fileInputRef.current) fileInputRef.current.value = '';  // added
  return;
}
```

The `finally` block already cleared the input on successful upload or upload error — this aligns the validation failure paths with that same behavior.

