Four UX issues in the token editing/generation workflow: token edit missing background removal, example tokens pre-selected by default, example gallery not wrapping, and no way to switch prompt language.

### Changes

- **Token edit background removal** — Added `removeBackground` checkbox + logic to `showTokenEditDialog`, matching existing behavior in the token generation dialog. Extended `_getCheckboxValue` with a `fallbackSelector` parameter to support both dialog contexts.

- **Example tokens default to unselected** — Removed `checked` from example checkbox inputs so users explicitly choose references.

- **Example gallery 4-per-row grid** — Replaced `display: flex` with `display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr)` on `.nanobanana-examples-gallery`. Removed fixed `width: 80px` from items.

- **Prompt description + language selector** — Added info box describing the token style (white background, gray circular base). Added Korean/English dropdown that swaps the default prompt text in the textarea. New i18n keys: `TokenGenDefaultPromptEN`, `TokenGenPromptDesc`, `TokenGenPromptLangLabel`, `TokenGenPromptLangKo`, `TokenGenPromptLangEn`.

```js
// Language selector wires up after dialog render with bounded retry
let _retryCount = 0;
const _wirePromptLangSelector = () => {
  const formEl = dialog.element?.querySelector?.("form.nanobanana-token-gen-dialog")
    ?? document.querySelector(".nanobanana-token-gen-dialog");
  if (!formEl) {
    if (++_retryCount < 20) setTimeout(_wirePromptLangSelector, 100);
    return;
  }
  // ...switches textarea between defaultPromptKo / defaultPromptEn
};
```

