The `TableRow` factory matched on `"Success"`/`"Issues"` status strings that no code path ever produces — `QueueRow.from(true, line)` emits `"Completed"` — so every completed row fell through to the `default` branch and received `queue-row-unknown` styling.

## Changes

- **`TableRow` switch**: replaced dead `case "Success"` with `case "Completed"`, removed dead `case "Issues"`
- **`removeAll` cleanup**: dropped unused `queue-row-issues` / `queue-status-issues` CSS class references from both the row factory and cell factory

```java
// Before — "Completed" rows always hit default:
case "Success":  getStyleClass().add("queue-row-success"); break;
case "Issues":   getStyleClass().add("queue-row-issues");  break;

// After — matches the actual status vocabulary:
case "Completed": getStyleClass().add("queue-row-success"); break;
```

The `installStatusCellFactory` already handled `"Completed"` correctly; only the row factory needed fixing.

