The middleware was calling `auth.protect()` unconditionally on all routes, causing a 500 for unauthenticated users hitting `/`. The page component already handles unauthenticated state gracefully (default name, zero progress).

- Use `createRouteMatcher(['/'])` to designate the home page as a public route
- Only call `auth.protect()` on non-public routes

```typescript
// Before
export default clerkMiddleware(async (auth) => {
  await auth.protect()
})

// After
const isPublicRoute = createRouteMatcher(['/'])

export default clerkMiddleware(async (auth, request) => {
  if (!isPublicRoute(request)) {
    await auth.protect()
  }
})
```

